cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "entities-gyre: the Gyre hexagon -- Sparks, Frames, the Debt Clock and the Commons"
abstract: >
  Entities are the simulated things and the actions on them, and this is the content
  and the drivers for one setting: rooms, NPCs, contracts, items. Setting and loop
  are RFD 0085, the Gyre, a MUD on the loot-action core-loop shell. It is not a new
  architecture -- the authoritative zone server is interactor-gyre, the client stays
  Godot unchanged, and transport lives on the ingest and gateway edges. The design
  constraint that decides everything else is that a companion and a player drive a
  Spark through the same surface, or the companion is a different game.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
