references:

  - type: report
    title: "RFD 0085: The Gyre -- a MUD setting on the loot-action core-loop shell"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    notes: >
      The setting and the loop this repository is content for. It already says NPC
      companions fill empty party slots when a party is short, which is the whole
      planner requirement in one line.

  - type: software
    title: "interactor-taskweft: the planner plane"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/interactor-taskweft"
    notes: >
      The HTN planner the RECTGTN ladder in docs/planner-ladder.md is written against.
      A driver here decides what a body should do; that repository decides how.

  - type: software
    title: "qwen38-mtp: the streaming probe kept as a throughput reference"
    notes: >
      sim/probe.py is that probe, unmodified. Kept rather than adapted so the measured
      MTP decode numbers in docs/mtp-measurements.md stay comparable to the source they
      came from, with the spec-off floor recorded beside them.
